From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: rx frame lengths, the PN check's lock, the silent
 hold's list

- A-MSDU: a first subframe too short for frame control or for the
  subframe header it starts with is dropped rather than compared with an
  LLC/SNAP header past its end.
- BAR: mt76_rx_aggr_check_ctl() needs the whole request (20 bytes) for
  its BAR control and starting sequence, not only the 16-byte header.
- connac2: the first fragment's 802.11 header is rebuilt only for a
  station's frame with an Ethernet header after the descriptor, and the
  MT7915's C-RXV word is read only in its branch of fill_rx_rate.
- PN: a frame of a TID with a BA session that the session didn't take
  (no-ack policy, before it started, while it stops) has its PN checked
  in mt76_rx_complete() under the session's lock, which its own frames
  are checked under (rx path, reorder work); a session stops and is
  drained before it is unlisted, so that lock is found until then.
- Silent hold: mt76_tx_result() orders the hold's fields, its flag and
  its silent_wait bit; the poll clears a bit before it looks again, at
  the slot's station now, so a station held (or added at a reused slot)
  meanwhile stays listed and is probed; with silent_hold off it unlists
  before it releases.
- record: the state is checked again after a device's first record
  (which can fill the buffer), memcpy only with something to copy,
  channels read under the lock.

KUnit for each, with seams where a window has to be hit
(mt76_tx_silent_unlisted, mt76_rx_pn_update) and a second CPU for the
session's stop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
